// twice-handler-nonidentity — the LOWERING gate for the re-exec driver.
//
// reexec-model.mn proves the DIRECT driver shape (run_twice(bt) hand-written)
// runs to 30. This proves the compiler must LOWER the handler form
// `{ body } ~> twice` INTO that shape — and that the continuation AFTER the
// perform (`+ 3`) survives each re-run, not just the identity case.
//
// body() = pick() + 3 → resume(v) re-runs body with pick→v = v + 3.
// arm sums two resumes: (10+3) + (20+3) = 13 + 23 = 36.
// The identity gate (mn-multishot, body()=pick()) proves the fork count;
// THIS proves the delimited continuation (the `+ 3`) is carried per fork.
//
// Exit 36 (< 127 — wasmtime aliases codes >=127 to 1; the harness must stay
// below the Unix signal wall, tests/native-cont/README.md).
//
// DORMANT TODAY (lower fabricates OneShot → LMakeContinuation, never called):
// exit is the one-shot 13 (first resume only), not 36. The band-B dig this
// gates: Hβ.lower.continuation-reification-codegen — yield-bubbling through
// the unified record: the MultiShot perform YIELDS, the frame's remainder
// reifies as a closure onto the k record, the install's driver binds k to the
// arm, resume(v) = call k (N times; immutable data). The `+ 3` here is exactly
// the remainder-closure the reification must carry per fork (PLAN §7 THE
// PIVOT; the AST-desugar and lower-synthesis forms are both refuted — the
// first erases the authored install from the graph, the second leaves the op
// singleton and re-enters the driver).
//
// Run (through a fixed m2):
//   MENTL_BOOT=.build/m2cache/m2.wasm tools/run-micro.sh \
//     tests/native-cont/twice-handler-nonidentity.mn 36 \
//     lib/runtime/memory.mn lib/runtime/strings.mn lib/runtime/lists.mn lib/prelude.mn

effect Pick { pick() -> Int }

handler twice with total = 0 {
  pick() => {
    let a = resume(10)
    let b = resume(20)
    a + b
  }
}

fn body() = pick() + 3

fn main(q) = { body() } ~> twice
